From: Trip Planner downstream experimental hardening
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] Preserve ASLR page offsets for glibc 2.41 thread arenas

Adapted from Ismael Ripoll and Hector Marco-Gisbert's 2020-03-25 v2
proposal for BZ 22853, https://sourceware.org/pipermail/libc-alpha/2020-March/112127.html
This is a downstream adaptation, not a claim of an accepted upstream fix.
The 2.41 adaptation replaces the correlated libc-address offset with the
existing direct non-cancelable kernel getrandom helper. Entropy failure
terminates initialization instead of weakening the offset. It uses runtime
heap_max_size, keeps cached mappings on the same grid, and initializes
after hugepage tunables so both explicit pages and fallback heaps satisfy
one header-lookup invariant. Linux x86_64 is the reviewed target.

